Note = {6th International Conference on Sheet Metal (SheMet 98), ENSCHEDE,
   NETHERLANDS, APR 06-08, 1998},
Abstract = {This paper shows some aspects of the design and control in logistic
   systems of typical processes in traditional integrated systems, IMS and
   virtual factories in the sheet metal industry. Main components of the
   virtual factory are logistics and the information technology background.
   By globalisation of production, factory inside logistics is replaced by
   a global logistic concept. In this paper those logistic concepts are
   summarised, which can be used in designing of material flow, optimising
   the parameters as well as in performance evaluation for closed loop
   production of sheet metal processing. The information flow, connected
   with the material flow, is also represented in the survey. Shared data
   structures and telecommunication are essential parts of the control
   strategy in logistic systems. (C) 2000 Elsevier Science S.A. All rights
